'''Transabyala AirFreight''' is a [[Balboa]]n {{w|cargo airline}} based at [[Portnou International Airport]] in [[Portnou]], [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. It operates scheduled and charter cargo services between Portnou and destinations across [[Lurandia]] and the [[Abyala]] region using a fleet of narrowbody freighter aircraft. The airline is privately owned and independent.

The airline's name derives from its operational focus: providing air freight connections across the Abyala region, linking the Portnou port complex — the [[Balboa Canal|canal]]'s Shendan terminus — with Lurandian and Abyalan destinations. Transabyala AirFreight is the only dedicated cargo airline based in Balboa.

== History ==

Transabyala AirFreight was founded in 2005 by a group of Portnou-based logistics entrepreneurs who identified a gap in the air cargo market between the canal port complex and the Lurandian and Abyalan regions. While the [[Balboa Canal]] handled the bulk of sea freight between the Shendan and Aethiopian coasts, a subset of cargo — perishable agricultural products, time-sensitive manufactured goods, and high-value items — required faster transit than sea shipping could provide. The founders recognised that [[Portnou International Airport]], with its proximity to the port and its 2003 introduction of international services, offered an ideal base for a dedicated cargo operation.

The airline commenced operations in 2005 with a single converted freighter, initially serving [[Tamsui International Airport|Tamsui]] and [[Gran Port de Sant Mateu International Airport|Gran Port de Sant Mateu]]. The route network expanded over the following years to include destinations across the Lurandian and Abyalan regions, reflecting the growing trade links between the Portnou port and neighbouring territories.

